<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Student materials on Llumàtics</title><link>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/privat/</link><description>Recent content in Student materials on Llumàtics</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/privat/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>B/W Film Development</title><link>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/revelat-bn/privat/doc/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/revelat-bn/privat/doc/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction"&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Black and white film development is the first step towards total control of the photographic process. Unlike colour developing, B/W is robust, forgiving and gives you enormous room to experiment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this workshop you have learned that there is no &amp;ldquo;correct&amp;rdquo; development — there is the development that best suits your photographic intention.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="history"&gt;History&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Photographic developing as we know it today has its roots in the 19th century. Fox Talbot described in 1839 the basic principle: light-sensitive silver salts are reduced to metallic silver in the presence of a reducing agent (the developer). Since then, the chemistry has evolved but the principle has not changed.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Student materials — Artisanal Developers</title><link>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/reveladors-artesanals/privat/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/reveladors-artesanals/privat/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Student materials — B/W Film Development</title><link>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/revelat-bn/privat/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/revelat-bn/privat/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Student materials — Beers Developer</title><link>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/copies-beers-developer/privat/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/copies-beers-developer/privat/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Student materials — Cianotípia</title><link>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/cianotipia/privat/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/cianotipia/privat/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Student materials — Còpies en paper</title><link>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/copies-en-paper/privat/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://112books.github.io/llumatics-web/en/tallers/copies-en-paper/privat/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Student materials — Del negatiu a la imatge — edició digital per a fotografia analògica</title><link>https: